  "evidence": "Arithmetic on published grades and project inventories; nothing is modelled. Chlorine grades are group means of CI chondrites (read in the compilations; one 2017 study, rejected by the compilers, gives a grade six times lower and is carried as a disputed low case) and the gas of one comet, 67P, which bounds a nucleus's chlorine from below. No body the project would mine has been assayed for chlorine. Shares assume every atom of chlorine in the processed feed is kept; the processing that would keep it is not designed. Lunar soil chlorine is inferred from a general statement, not measured values. The sea's need is its fill at seawater's strength, without the salt the crust takes with the water it draws from the floor.",
  "reading_rule": "Masses in kg; shares are of the South Pole-Aitken Sea's chloride at seawater's strength unless named otherwise. low, central and high follow the grade's range; a two-entry list is (low, high). In riding, each route gives the chlorine carried by all of that import if it came wholly from that kind of body; the routes are alternatives for one import and add across imports. Near-Earth asteroid figures are upper bounds at carbonaceous grades.",
